openwizdev/WizSite/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/deployments","created_at":"2026-11-15T01:10:49Z","updated_at":"2026-11-20T09:38:50Z","pushed_at":"2026-11-24T14:33:09Z","git_url":"git://github.com/openwizdev/WizSite.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:openwizdev/WizSite.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/openwizdev/WizSite.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/openwizdev/WizSite","homepage":"","size":205874,"stargazers_count":1,"watchers_count":1,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":0,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":61,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["agent-factory","cloudflare-pages","landing-page","open-source","static-site","website"],"visibility":"public","forks":0,"open_issues":61,"watchers":1,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":true,"maintain":true,"push":true,"triage":true,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/pulls/181","html_url":"https://github.com/openwizdev/WizSite/pull/181","diff_url":"https://github.com/openwizdev/WizSite/pull/181.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/openwizdev/WizSite/pull/181.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-24T12:15:27Z"},"body":"Implements openwizdev/OpenWiz#2967 (BK4 of spec #2963): `/book`, the OpenWiz booking page and its installable progressive web app.\n\n## What was built\n\n- **Booking page (`book/index.html`, `book/book.css`, `book/book.js`)**:\n  - OpenWiz dark design (`tokens.css` + `site.css` + `book/book.css`), Geist typography, brass CTA, phone-first responsive layout, zero frameworks, no inline script or style, text contrast 7.93:1–15.21:1 (>= 4.5:1).\n  - Loads `GET /api/book/slots` and opens with the first day that has open times selected and its times visible as >= 48 px tap targets in the visitor’s own time zone (with the IANA zone named).\n  - 14-day picker: days with no open times are dimmed and `disabled` (skipped by Tab and ArrowLeft/ArrowRight/Home/End keyboard navigation).\n  - Tapping a time opens the in-place form (`name`, `email`, `team`, plus off-screen `website` honeypot with `tabindex=\"-1\"`, `autocomplete=\"off\"`, not `display: none`) and submits `POST /api/book` with `tz`.\n  - Inline field validation moves focus to the first invalid field and announces updates via `aria-live`.\n  - Confirmation in place shows the booked time, `\"A confirmation is on its way to <email>.\"` (or `\"You’re booked. Save the time below.\"` when `email !== \"sent\"`), an **Add to calendar** button downloading an `.ics` generated in the browser, and a one-line install hint.\n  - All states handled: quiet loading skeleton (reduced motion respected), no open times, `slot_taken` (409 alert, reloads slots, keeps typed form values), `rate_limited` (429), `unavailable` (503 plain line + `/team/` link, no `mailto:`), and offline shell.\n  - Cancel flow: `/book/?cancel=<id>.<token>` immediately strips the token with `history.replaceState`, prompts `\"Cancel this call?\"` with one button posting to `POST /api/book/cancel`, then shows `\"Cancelled\"` and a link to book again.\n- **Installable PWA (`book/manifest.webmanifest`, `book/sw.js`, `book/icon-192.png`, `book/icon-512.png`, `book/icon-maskable-512.png`)**:\n  - Manifest `\"Book OpenWiz\"`, `id`/`start_url`/`scope: \"/book/\"`, `display: \"standalone\"`, `#1b1916` ground, 192 px, 512 px, and maskable 512 px PNG icons rendered from the existing brand mark.\n  - Service worker scoped to `/book/`: network-first for the page shell, caches shell and static assets (CSS, JS, fonts, icons), explicitly skips `/api/`, and prunes old caches on `activate`.\n  - `@media (display-mode: standalone)` hides the site top bar and footer.\n- **Site wiring & checks**:\n  - `build.mjs` builds and fingerprints `book/index.html`, `book/book.css`, `book/book.js`, and copies the manifest, service worker, and icons.\n  - `_headers` enforces strict CSP on `/book/*` (`connect-src 'self'`, `worker-src 'self'`, `manifest-src 'self'`, `form-action 'none'`, `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`, `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`).\n  - `scripts/check.py` + `scripts/test_check.py` verify the page, manifest, service worker, CSP, pinned icon hashes, copy, absence of price/cost words, form actions, and that no other page links to `/book` yet.\n  - `docs/maintaining.md` adds **The booking page** paragraph. `team/index.html` is untouched.\n  - `scripts/book-check.mjs` + `scripts/book-fixtures/slots.json` run headless Chromium over CDP at 390 px and 1280 px across every state, keyboard path, cancel view, offline shell, and Chrome installability (`Page.getAppManifest` + `Page.getInstallabilityErrors`).\n\n## Proof\n\n- **Proof first** (`d247242`): added `test_book_page` in `scripts/test_check.py` and `scripts/book-check.mjs`; confirmed red (`FileNotFoundError` for `book/index.html`).\n- **Full verification** (`82463c8`):\n\n```text\n> npm run build\nStatic site: 114 public files in dist/ (..., book/book.781213c4b4.css, book/book.f4ceb305ba.js, ...)\n\n> npm run check\nPASS: pinned WebP artwork and spec recording within budget; the launch video within its own budget\nPASS: exact export, local links/fragments, CSS resources, fonts/licences, copy and privacy\n\n> npm test\n.......................................................\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 55 tests in 242.697s\n\nOK\n\n> node scripts/book-check.mjs --shots /tmp/book-shots\nPASS: book-check (390px, 1280px, keyboard, states, cancel, installability, offline)\n\n> python3 -I tools/comment-check/check.py diff --base origin/book\ncomment-check: ok\n```\n\n- **Chrome installability check**: `Page.getAppManifest` returned 0 errors, `Page.getInstallabilityErrors` returned `[]`, and `navigator.serviceWorker.ready` activated at scope `/book/` inside `scripts/book-check.mjs`.\n- **Screenshots generated** by `node scripts/book-check.mjs --shots <dir>` (visually inspected at 390 px and 1280 px, zero horizontal overflow):\n  - Phone (390 px): `phone-picker.png`, `phone-form.png`, `phone-confirmation.png`, `phone-unavailable.png`\n  - Desktop (1280 px): `desktop-picker.png`, `desktop-form.png`, `desktop-confirmation.png`, `desktop-unavailable.png`\n\nBuilt with [Cloudroom](https://cloudroom.dev)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/issues/181/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/issues/181/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"actor":{"login":"jparker2006","id